-- title:
--   Transition law and images of the unramified-layer quotient charts
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $r$ is a prime number.
--
--   **Coefficients.** $\mathcal{O}$ is a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), $\pi \in \mathcal{O}$ is irreducible (`hπ`), $\mathcal{O}$ is $\pi$-adically complete (`hcomplete`), the residue ring $\mathcal{O}/\pi$ has exactly $r$ elements (`hres`), and $r$ and $\pi$ generate the same ideal (`hunr`). $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero field which is the fraction field of $\mathcal{O}$.
--
--   **Unramified layer.** $\mathit{Onr}$ is a characteristic-zero domain and $\mathcal{O}$-algebra with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, subject to: $\mathit{Onr}$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`), that ideal is maximal (`hOnr_max`), every element of $\mathit{Onr}$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal{O}$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial over $\mathit{Onr}$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi}$ for all $x$ (`hFr`).
--
--   **Valuation of the determinant.** $\mathrm{vdet} : GL_2(K_0) \to \mathbb{Z}$ (written multiplicatively) is a homomorphism such that $\mathrm{vdet}(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\pi^{n}$ in $K_0$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal{O}$ (`hvdet`).
--
--   **Group data.** $G$ is a group with a homomorphism $\sigma : G \to GL_2(K_0)$ and a subgroup $\Gamma$ such that some $z \in \Gamma$ has $\sigma z$ a scalar matrix with $\mathrm{vdet}(\sigma z) = 2$ (`hcent`) and some $w \in \Gamma$ has $\mathrm{vdet}(\sigma w) = 1$ (`hodd`); $\Gamma'$ is a subgroup characterised by $x \in \Gamma' \iff x \in \Gamma$ and $\mathrm{vdet}(\sigma x)$ even (`hΓ'`). The homomorphism $\rho : G \to PGL_2(K_0)$ sends $g$ to the class of $\sigma g$ (`hρ`); the image $\rho(\Gamma')$ acts on the set of homothety classes of full lattices ([`LT.LatticeTree.Vertex`](def/LatticeTreeOrbital.html#L349)) with finite vertex stabilisers (`hdisc`) and with a finite set of vertices meeting every orbit (`hcocpt`). The matrix $g_1$ is $\mathrm{diag}(\pi,1)$ (`hg₁`).
--
--   **Mumford tower.** $N$ is a subgroup of $PGL_2(K_0)$ contained in $\rho(\Gamma')$ (`hNle`), normal as a subgroup of $\rho(\Gamma)$ (`hNnorm`), and of non-zero relative index in $\rho(\Gamma')$ (`hNidx`); $DM$ is a `MumfordTower 𝒪 π K₀ r g₁ N`, that is, schemes $Z_n$ proper and flat over $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+1})$ with cartesian transition maps $zt_n$, affine neighbourhoods of finite subsets, together with a system of maps $q_n$ from the Deligne-datum functor `Omega K₀ π` (whose $B$-points assign to each full lattice a $B$-submodule of its base change with invertible quotient, compatibly with inclusions and homotheties, and non-degenerately at each prime) into $Z_n$, natural in $B$, compatible with the base and the transitions, invariant under the elements of $N$, and equipped with chart open immersions.
--
--   **The tower $X$ and its structure.** $X : \mathbb{N} \to \mathbf{Sch}$ comes with structure maps $xb_n : X_n \to \mathrm{Spec}(\mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+1})$ and transitions $xt_n : X_n \to X_{n+1}$, a finite group $G_2$ acting by $a_n : G_2 \to \mathrm{Aut}(X_n)$, and projections $pr_{1,n} : X_n \to Z_n$ and $pr_{2,n} : X_n \to \mathrm{Spec}(\mathcal{O}_2/\pi^{n+1})$, where $\mathcal{O}_2 =$ `AlgHom.equalizer` of $\mathrm{Fr}\circ\mathrm{Fr}$ and the identity, i.e. the subring of $\mathit{Onr}$ fixed by $\mathrm{Fr}^2$. Further data are a homomorphism $\theta : \Gamma \to G_2$ and $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphisms $\mathrm{Fr}_{2,n}$ of $\mathcal{O}_2/\pi^{n+1}$. The hypotheses on these are: the squares formed by $xt_n$, $xb_n$, $xb_{n+1}$ and the reduction $\mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+2} \to \mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+1}$ are pullbacks (`hcart`); each $xb_n$ is proper (`hproper`) and flat (`hflat`); every finite subset of $X_n$ lies in an affine open (`haff`); the $G_2$-action is over the base (`ha_over`) and commutes with the transitions (`ha_xt`); $X_n$ is the fibre product of $Z_n$ and $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathcal{O}_2/\pi^{n+1})$ over $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+1})$, via $pr_{1,n}$, $pr_{2,n}$, $zb_n$ and the map induced by $\mathcal{O} \to \mathcal{O}_2$ (`hX`); $xb_n = pr_{1,n}$ followed by $zb_n$ (`hxb`); the projections commute with the transitions (`hxt₁`, `hxt₂`); $\theta$ is surjective (`hθsurj`) with $\theta\gamma = 1$ if and only if $\rho\gamma \in N$ (`hθker`); $\mathrm{Fr}_{2,n}$ is induced by $\mathrm{Fr}$ on $\mathcal{O}_2$ (`hFr₂`); the automorphism $a_n(\theta\gamma)$ acts on $pr_{2,n}$ by the $\bigl(-\mathrm{vdet}(\sigma\gamma)\bigr)$-th power of $\mathrm{Fr}_{2,n}$ (`ha_pr₂`); and, for $\gamma \in \Gamma$, $B$ an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra in which $\pi^{n+1} = 0$, and Deligne data $P, P'$ over $B$ with $P'$ the pullback of $P$ along $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$ in the sense of `DeligneDatum.IsPullback` (lattice-wise, $P'$'s line is the comap of $P$'s line at the translated lattice), any $x : \mathrm{Spec}\,B \to X_n$ with $x$ followed by $pr_{1,n}$ equal to $DM.q_n(P)$ satisfies: $x$ followed by $a_n(\theta\gamma)$ and then $pr_{1,n}$ equals $DM.q_n(P')$ (`ha_pr₁`).
--
--   **Quotient tower.** $DQ$ is a `TowerQuotientDatum 𝒪 π X xb xt G₂ a`: schemes $Y_n$, proper and flat over $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+1})$ with cartesian transitions $yt_n$, together with maps $p_n : X_n \to Y_n$ over the base, compatible with the transitions and cartesian over them, invariant under $G_2$, finite, surjective, locally epimorphic, and satisfying a local universal property. The maps $q_n$ send, for $B$ an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra with $\pi^{n+1} = 0$, a pair consisting of an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $\mathit{Onr} \to B$ and a Deligne datum over $B$ (the $B$-points of `AlgFunctor.prod (AlgFunctor.corep Onr) (Omega K₀ π)`) to a morphism $\mathrm{Spec}\,B \to Y_n$. They are subject to: a characterisation in terms of $X_n$ — if $\psi : \mathit{Onr} \to B$, $\psi_2 : \mathcal{O}_2/\pi^{n+1} \to B$ agrees with $\psi$ on $\mathcal{O}_2$, $P$ is a Deligne datum over $B$ and $x : \mathrm{Spec}\,B \to X_n$ has $x$ followed by $pr_{1,n}$ equal to $DM.q_n(P)$ and $x$ followed by $pr_{2,n}$ equal to $\mathrm{Spec}(\psi_2)$, then $q_n(\psi,P) = x$ followed by $p_n$ (`hqdef`); compatibility with the base (`hqover`); naturality in $B$ (`hqnat`); compatibility with the transitions $yt_n$ (`hqyt`); and invariance: for $\gamma \in \Gamma$ and $B$-points $x, x'$ related by `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` for $\sigma\gamma$ — the $\mathit{Onr}$-component of $x'$ is the $\bigl(-\mathrm{vdet}(\sigma\gamma)\bigr)$-fold Frobenius twist of that of $x$, and the Deligne data are related by pullback along $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$ — one has $q_n(x') = q_n(x)$ (`hqinv`).
--
--   **Unramified presentation and its quotient.** $\mathit{Pr}$ is a `MumfordTower.NrPresentation` for the above data with subgroup $E = \theta(\Gamma' \cap \Gamma)$: schemes $X'_n$ over $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathit{Onr}/\pi^{n+1})$ with cartesian transitions, a $G_2$-action $a'_n$ over the base, maps $qX_n : X'_n \to X_n$ exhibiting $X'_n$ as the base change of $X_n$ along $\mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+1} \to \mathit{Onr}/\pi^{n+1}$ and commuting with the transitions and with the actions, and charts $\kappa'_{h,n} : \mathrm{Spec}\bigl(A/\pi^{n+1}\bigr) \to X'_n$ indexed by $h \in GL_2(K_0)$, where $A =$ `chartERing Onr (algebraMap 𝒪 Onr π) r` is the localisation of $\mathit{Onr}[x_0,x_1]$ modulo the edge relation away from the discriminant element, together with the axioms relating these charts to $pr_1$ and the rest of the structure. $D'$ is a `TowerQuotientDatum` for the tower $(\mathit{Pr}.X', \mathit{Pr}.xb', \mathit{Pr}.xt')$ over $\mathit{Onr}$ with uniformiser the image of $\pi$ and $G_2$-action $\mathit{Pr}.a'$; the morphisms $rY_n : D'.Y_n \to DQ.Y_n$ exhibit $D'.Y_n$ as the base change of $DQ.Y_n$ along $\mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+1} \to \mathit{Onr}/\pi^{n+1}$ (`hrY`), satisfy $D'.p_n$ followed by $rY_n$ equals $\mathit{Pr}.qX_n$ followed by $DQ.p_n$ (`hrY_p`), and commute with the transitions: $D'.yt_n$ followed by $rY_{n+1}$ equals $rY_n$ followed by $DQ.yt_n$ (`hrY_yt`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** Writing $\lambda_{h,n} = \kappa'_{h,n}$ followed by $D'.p_n$, a morphism $\mathrm{Spec}(A/\pi^{n+1}) \to D'.Y_n$, the assertion is the conjunction of the following two statements, each for every $h \in GL_2(K_0)$ and every $n \in \mathbb{N}$.
--
--   (i) $\lambda_{h,n}$ followed by $D'.yt_n$ equals $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the reduction $A/\pi^{n+2} \to A/\pi^{n+1}$ (the map `Ideal.Quotient.factor` for the inclusion of the ideal generated by the $(n+2)$-nd power of the image of $\pi$ in $A$ into the ideal generated by its $(n+1)$-st power), followed by $\lambda_{h,n+1}$.
--
--   (ii) The range of the underlying continuous map of $\lambda_{h,n}$ equals the preimage, under the underlying continuous map of $D'.yt_n$, of the range of the underlying continuous map of $\lambda_{h,n+1}$.
--
--   This records, for the quotient of the unramified layer of the formal Mumford/Čerednik–Drinfeld tower, that the images of the charts are compatible with the transition maps both as morphisms and on underlying point sets, the latter identifying the chart image at level $n$ as the exact preimage of the chart image at level $n+1$. It is used in the construction of the descended quotient charts ([`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_nrCharts`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_nrCharts)) and in the analysis of sections of functions on the quotient ([`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_nrFunctions_sections_of_inv`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_nrFunctions_sections_of_inv)), and rests on the corresponding statement for the charts of $\mathit{Pr}$ before passing to the quotient ([`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_nrCharts_kappa_transition`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_nrCharts_kappa_transition)).
